  "source": "source/md/<file>, byte-identical to the pandoc 2.9.2.1 `--to gfm --wrap=none` conversion of source/docx/<same stem>.docx",
  "method": "Measured, not authored. Two scans per file, each in DOCUMENT ORDER. (1) `brackets`: every match of /\\\\\\[.*?\\\\\\]/ — pandoc escapes the form's square brackets as \\\\[ … \\\\] — plus the single brace placeholder {. . .} in the Singapore form, merged into one list by byte offset. Every backslash-escaped bracket in all ten files is accounted for: the count of '\\\\[' equals the count of '\\\\]' equals the number of matches, in every file, and no unescaped […] survives the conversion. (2) `blanks`: every <u></u> whose content is whitespace only. The form also uses <u> to underline sub-headings (\"Equity Financing\", \"excluding\"), and those are NOT blanks and are excluded by the whitespace test. Hole names for brackets come from the placeholder literal; the underscore runs are ambiguous on their literal alone and are resolved by the sentence they sit in (\"THIS CERTIFIES THAT\" -> purchaseAmount, \"Post-Money Valuation Cap\" -> valuationCap, \"Province of\"/\"Courts of\" -> governingProvince). Hole names for blanks come from the label printed immediately before the blank on the same line (By: / Name: / Title: / Address: / Email:, empty = a continuation of the line above) and from which side of the INVESTOR heading the blank falls on.",
  "vocabulary": {
    "companyName": "The company's legal name, as printed in running text (title case in the placeholder).",
    "companyNameCaps": "The same value, at a position whose placeholder is upper case (cover title, signature block, letterhead). Same input, different rendering; see placeholder_case.",
    "investorName": "The investor's legal name, in running text.",
    "investorNameCaps": "The same value at an upper-case position. Occurs only in the side letters' signature block.",
    "purchaseAmount": "The amount the investor pays, in the currency the form prints before the blank ($ on the US forms, US$ on SG/CA/KY).",
    "dateOfSafe": "The date of the instrument (\"on or about\").",
    "stateOfIncorporation": "US forms only: the state under whose law the company is incorporated.",
    "incorporationJurisdiction": "Canada only: the placeholder reads \"Canada / Applicable Province\", i.e. the drafter expects EITHER the federal jurisdiction OR a province, not both.",
    "companyRegistrationNumber": "Singapore only, and NOT a bracket: the form prints \"Company Registration number {. . .}\". It is the only brace-delimited hole in the whole corpus.",
    "valuationCap": "The Post-Money Valuation Cap. Absent from the discount and MFN forms.",
    "discountRate": "US discount form only. The placeholder is \"[100 minus the discount]%\", so the filled value is the RATE (80 for a 20% discount), not the discount.",
    "governingLaw": "US forms only: the state whose law governs (\"the laws of the State of [___]\"). The SG and KY forms fix Singapore and the Cayman Islands respectively and have no such hole.",
    "governingProvince": "Canada only: the province, filled TWICE on one line (\"laws of the Province of [___]\" and \"Courts of [___]\"). One value, two occurrences.",
    "companySignatoryName": "Printed name of the person signing for the company; the placeholder is the italic word [name].",
    "companySignatoryTitle": "Title of that person; placeholder [title].",
    "investorSignatoryName": "Printed name of the person signing for the investor. NOT a bracket: an underlined blank after \"Name:\".",
    "investorSignatoryTitle": "Title of that person; an underlined blank after \"Title:\".",
    "companySignatureLine": "The company's manuscript signature line, an underlined blank after \"By:\". Not a fill-in for the generator; recorded so the positional map is complete and nothing is silently skipped.",
    "investorSignatureLine": "The investor's manuscript signature line, likewise.",
    "companyAddress": "First line of the company's notice address; an underlined blank after \"Address:\".",
